# Stop buggy code before it reaches GitHub.
#
# Fast tier only, scoped to what changed — typically well under two minutes. CI still runs the
# full suite, coverage ratchet, contract drift and the journey stack after the push lands.
#
# Bypass with `git push --no-verify` when you genuinely need to (pushing a WIP branch for a
# colleague, say). Bypassing to get a red gate out of the way is how the gate stops meaning
# anything, so if it fires, read it.
cd "$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)"
./scripts/quality/gate.sh
